<!-- SECTION 2: OVERVIEW / INTRO + TL;DR -->
<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">FSSAI State License in Delhi - At a Glance</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - FSSAI State License in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>FSSAI State License in Delhi is mandatory for food businesses with turnover Rs 12 lakh-Rs 20 crore operating within Delhi. Applied via Form B on FoSCoS portal (foscos.fssai.gov.in). Fee: Rs 2,000-5,000/year. Approved by Designated Officer, Delhi Food Safety Dept. 25-30 working days processing. <a href="/fssai-registration">FSSAI Registration across India</a>.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi requires THREE co-licenses for dine-in restaurants: FSSAI State License + Eating House License (Delhi Police) + Health Trade License (MCD/NDMC). One FSSAI license covers one premises only. Multi-brand cloud kitchens can endorse up to 10 brands on one State License.</p>
                <p>The FSSAI Northern Region office is headquartered at FDA Bhawan, Kotla Road, New Delhi. For new food businesses below Rs 12 lakh turnover, <a href="/fssai-registration">FSSAI Registration</a> (Basic) applies. For businesses above Rs 20 crore or multi-state, <a href="/fssai-central-license">FSSAI Central License</a> is required.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is an FSSAI State License?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>FSSAI State License in Delhi is the food safety authorization issued under Section 31 of the FSS Act, 2006 to FBOs with turnover Rs 12 lakh-Rs 20 crore operating within Delhi. Issued by the Designated Officer, Department of Food Safety, Government of NCT of Delhi on Form B filed through FoSCoS portal. Every licensed FBO receives a unique 14-digit FSSAI number.</p>
                    <p>The State License sits in the middle tier: above Basic Registration (below Rs 12 lakh) and below Central License (above Rs 20 crore or multi-state). One FSSAI State License covers exactly one premises address - multi-outlet Delhi chains need separate licenses per branch.</p>
                    <p>Delhi cloud kitchens benefit from a unique provision: a single State License can endorse up to 10 different food brands from one kitchen address. For complete food business compliance, <a href="/gst-registration">GST Registration</a> and <a href="/shop-act-registration">Shop Act Registration</a> are also essential.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for FSSAI State License in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Form B:</strong> Application form for State and Central License on FoSCoS portal. Requires business details, food categories, premises address, FSMS plan.</p><p><strong>Kind of Business (KoB):</strong> FSSAI classification determining eligibility tier and fee. Wrong KoB selection causes application rejection.</p><p><strong>FSMS Plan:</strong> Food Safety Management System plan - mandatory for State License. Covers hazard analysis, hygiene, pest control, employee health.</p><p><strong>Schedule 4:</strong> FSSAI hygiene and sanitation requirements checked during premises inspection by Delhi Food Safety Officers.</p><p><strong>Tatkal Issuance:</strong> Expedited/instant license issuance available on FoSCoS for eligible Delhi FBO categories requiring immediate operations start.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
