<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal Framework for FSSAI State License in Delhi</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul><li><strong>FSS Act, 2006 - Section 31:</strong> Mandatory license/registration for all FBOs. Section 63: penalty up to Rs 5 lakh + imprisonment up to 6 months.</li><li><strong>FSS (Licensing and Registration) Regulations, 2011:</strong> Three-tier framework, fee schedule, Form A/B, validity 1-5 years. <a href="https://foscos.fssai.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FoSCoS Portal</a></li><li><strong>Delhi NCT - Food Safety Commissioner:</strong> Heads Department of Food Safety (foodsafety.delhi.gov.in). Oversees all DOs who approve State Licenses. <a href="https://foodsafety.delhi.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi Food Safety</a></li><li><strong>Delhi NCT - Eating House License:</strong> Delhi Police Act requires separate Eating House License for all dine-in restaurants alongside FSSAI.</li><li><strong>Delhi NCT - Health Trade License:</strong> MCD/NDMC issues Health Trade License - third co-requirement for Delhi restaurants.</li><li><strong>Annual Return - Form D-1:</strong> Food manufacturers file by 31 May each year. Non-filing affects renewal. <a href="https://fssai.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FSSAI Official</a></li></ul>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

